P(A and B) = P(A)·P(B|A); for independent events, P(A)·P(B). P(A or B) = P(A)+P(B)−P(A and B). Worked example: two independent deploys each fail with p=0.1. P(both fail) = 0.1×0.1 = **0.010000000000000002**. P(at least one fails) = 1 − P(neither) = 1 − 0.9² = **0.19**. Complement-first ('1 minus the boring case') solves most 'at least one' problems. Independence is an assumption to check, not a default: correlated failures break the multiplication.

